# A Generic Data Fetcher

Create a composable that handles loading, error, and data states for any API call.

```javascript
import { ref } from 'vue'

export function useFetch(url) {
  const data = ref(null)
  const loading = ref(false)
  const error = ref(null)

  const fetchData = async () => {
    loading.value = true
    try {
      const res = await fetch(url)
      data.value = await res.json()
    } catch (err) {
      error.value = err
    } finally {
      loading.value = false
    }
  }

  fetchData() // execute immediately

  return { data, loading, error, refetch: fetchData }
}
```

This can be reused for any API endpoint.

# Combining Composables

Composables can call other composables, enabling powerful compositions.

```javascript
export function useUserProfile(userId) {
  const { data: user, loading, error } = useFetch(`/api/users/${userId}`)
  const { data: posts } = useFetch(`/api/users/${userId}/posts`)
  // ... additional logic
  return { user, posts, loading, error }
}
```

This keeps each composable focused and testable.

Composables can return promises, but remember that `setup()` cannot be async. Instead, handle async operations inside the composable and expose reactive state that updates when the promise resolves.

For async initialization, you can use `onMounted` inside the composable.

```javascript
export function useAsyncData(loader) {
  const data = ref(null)
  const loading = ref(true)
  onMounted(async () => {
    data.value = await loader()
    loading.value = false
  })
  return { data, loading }
}
```
